{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-500388d0-cf26-46df-a7d4-4749fbf6b12b","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b696c9acbc5fe684","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9017-v52w7mzf/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9017-E001.md","content":"# Keyboard accessibility remediation for the four audited Dashboard flows\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the keyboard accessibility fixes for the four core Dashboard\nflows identified by the accessibility audit — project creation, workbench\nspawn, model deployment, and pipeline run submission — so that each flow is\nfully operable by keyboard alone, with no focus traps, no unreachable\ncontrols, and consistent visible focus indicators. The audit report enumerates\nthe exact defects per flow; this epic resolves every enumerated defect.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Remediate all keyboard-operability defects the audit enumerated across the\n  four audited flows:\n  - project creation\n  - workbench spawn\n  - model deployment\n  - pipeline run submission\n- Eliminate focus loss and focus traps in the modals used by the audited\n  flows (focus must return to the invoking control when a modal closes, and\n  must remain within the modal while it is open).\n- Make every interactive control in the audited flows reachable and operable\n  via keyboard traversal.\n- Apply consistent visible focus indicators across the audited flows, per the\n  audit's indicator findings, so focus state is uniformly detectable.\n- Add regression coverage (automated where practical, otherwise a documented\n  manual keyboard-walkthrough checklist) for the fixed defects so the flows\n  cannot silently regress.\n\nOut of scope: screen-reader semantics beyond what the keyboard fixes require,\nand flows outside the four audited ones (per the strategy's Out of Scope).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Each of the four audited flows can be completed end to end using keyboard\n  input only, verified by a walkthrough against the audit report's defect\n  list, with every enumerated defect for those flows marked resolved.\n- No focus traps remain in the audited flows: focus contained within open\n  modals and restored to the invoking control on close, verified per the\n  audit's enumerated modal defects.\n- No unreachable controls remain in the audited flows: every interactive\n  control is reachable and operable by keyboard, verified per the audit's\n  enumerated reachability defects.\n- Focus indicators are visibly consistent across all controls in the audited\n  flows, verified per the audit's indicator findings.\n- Regression coverage for the fixed defects exists and passes.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 (P1)** — The four audited core flows are fully operable by\n  keyboard, with no focus traps or unreachable controls: covered by the\n  keyboard-operability, focus-trap, and reachability scope above.\n- **HLR-2 (P1)** — Visible focus indicators are consistent across the audited\n  flows: covered by the focus-indicator scope above. Bundled with HLR-1\n  because both are resolved by the same remediation sweep over the same UI\n  surfaces enumerated by the audit; a separate epic would revisit every\n  already-fixed surface.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":25401,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-97fb1fb4ecf1dbad","agent_id":"a94a72592b85fae6b","session_id":"5c3c65cc-0035-4892-89e3-f0c9961f403f","uuid":"e59ef926-8ba6-4985-b21f-7deb1b159913","timestamp":"2026-10-26T14:21:17.649Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9017"}
