lows reachable and operable\n52\t  via keyboard traversal.\n53\t- Apply consistent visible focus indicators across the audited flows, per the\n54\t  audit's indicator findings, so focus state is uniformly detectable.\n55\t- Add regression coverage (automated where practical, otherwise a documented\n56\t  manual keyboard-walkthrough checklist) for the fixed defects so the flows\n57\t  cannot silently regress.\n58\t\n59\tOut of scope: screen-reader semantics beyond what the keyboard fixes require,\n60\tand flows outside the four audited ones (per the strategy's Out of Scope).\n61\t\n62\t## Acceptance Criteria\n63\t\n64\t- Each of the four audited flows can be completed end to end using keyboard\n65\t  input only, verified by a walkthrough against the audit report's defect\n66\t  list, with every enumerated defect for those flows marked resolved.\n67\t- No focus traps remain in the audited flows: focus contained within open\n68\t  modals and restored to the invoking control on close, verified per the\n69\t  audit's enumerated modal defects.\n70\t- No unreachable controls remain in the audited flows: every interactive\n71\t  control is reachable and operable by keyboard, verified per the audit's\n72\t  enumerated reachability defects.\n73\t- Focus indicators are visibly consistent across all controls in the audited\n74\t  flows, verified per the audit's indicator findings.\n75\t- Regression coverage for the fixed defects exists and passes.\n76\t\n77\t## HLR Traceability\n78\t\n79\t- **HLR-1 (P1)** — The four audited core flows are fully operable by\n80\t  keyboard, with no focus traps or unreachable controls: covered by the\n81\t  keyboard-operability, focus-trap, and reachability scope above.\n82\t- **HLR-2 (P1)** — Visible focus indicators are consistent across the audited\n83\t  flows: covered by the focus-indicator scope above. Bundled with HLR-1\n84\t  because both are resolved by the same remediation sweep over the same UI\n85\t  surfaces enumerated by the audit; 